\par 1. The Main "Containers"
\par While the List<T> is the most common, there are others designed for specific logic:
\par 
\par List<T>: The "Dynamic Array." Best for general use when you need to add/remove items.
\par 
\par Dictionary<TKey, TValue>: A "Hash Map." It stores data in Key-Value pairs (like a real dictionary where the "Key" is the word and the "Value" is the definition).
\par 
\par HashSet<T>: A collection of unique items. It\rquote s incredibly fast for checking if an item exists and automatically prevents duplicates.
\par 
\par Stack<T>: Last-In-First-Out (LIFO). Think of a stack of plates\emdash you add to the top and take from the top.
\par 
\par Queue<T>: First-In-First-Out (FIFO). Like a line at a store\emdash first person in is the first person served.
\par 
