\par 
\par For Adding and Removing:
\par .Add(item): Puts an item at the end.
\par 
\par .Insert(index, item): Squeezes an item into a specific spot.
\par 
\par .Remove(item): Finds the first match and deletes it.
\par 
\par .RemoveAt(index): Deletes whatever is at that specific position.
\par 
\par .Clear(): Wipes the entire collection clean.
\par 
\par For Searching and Checking:
\par .Contains(item): Returns true or false.
\par 
\par .IndexOf(item): Returns the position of an item.
\par 
\par .ContainsKey(key): (Specific to Dictionaries) Checks if a specific key exists.
\par 
\par For Organizing:
\par .Sort(): Sorts the list in-place (no Array.Sort needed!).
\par 
\par .Reverse(): Flips the list in-place.
\par 
\par .Find(x => ...): Finds the first item that matches a specific condition.
